{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "#4 - Configure the user profile policy and enable SSR",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Lab Overview",
      "description": "## Configure the user profile policy and enable SSR\n\n 🎯 **Objective**    Configure the user profile policy and enable self-service registration for an application.\n\n  🎬 **Scenario**   Algen Scoop Shop wants customers to be able to sign up for their app with an invitation code. Now that the needed profile attribute has been added to the user profile, we need to update the sign-up form and enable self-service registration in the profile policy."
    },
    {
      "title": "Create a user profile policy",
      "description": "## Create a user profile policy\n\n1. From the Okta Admin Dashboard, go to **Security** > **User Profile Policies**.\n\n2. Select **Add user profile policy**.\n\n3. Name this policy **Customer policy**.\n\n4. Select **Save**."
    },
    {
      "title": "Enable self-service registration in the profile enrollment policy",
      "description": "## Enable self-service registration in the profile enrollment policy\n1. Select the **pencil icon** next to the policy you just created (Customer policy).\n\n1. You are now on the Enrollment tab. In the Profile Enrollment section, select the **Edit** link.\n\n2. Notice that **Self-service registration** is already set to **Allowed** in this policy. Keep it this way and stay on this page.\n\n4. Next to **Add the user to group**, enter and select **Customers** (Note: If you do not have this group, you need to complete the steps in the Prerequisites section of this lab).\n\n5. Scroll down and select **Save**."
    },
    {
      "title": "Configure the profile enrollment form",
      "description": "## Configure the profile enrollment form\n\nThe profile enrollment form is the sign-up form that will be rendered in the Okta Sign-in Widget during the self-service registration flow.\n\n1. Still on the Enrollment tab, scroll down to the **Profile enrollment form**.\n\n2. Notice that since the **Invitation Code** is required, it has automatically been added to the form, so no further action is needed.",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 4
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 2,
          "character": 1
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Add an application to the policy",
      "description": "## Add an application to the policy\n\n1. Now select the **Apps** tab on this page.\n\n2. Select **Add an App to this Policy**.\n\n3. Next to **Customer Rewards**, select **Apply**. Note: If you do not have this app, you need to complete the steps in the Prerequisites section of this lab.\n\n5. Select **Close**.",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 4
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 36
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Test self-service registration",
      "description": "## Test self-service registration\n\nBefore following the directions below, that ensure you are **logged out** of any Okta sessions. **DO NOT use an Incognito browser window** for the steps that follow.\n\n1. Select [this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\" python3 -m http.server 8080\"]) to run Algen Scoop Shop's app. Once the web server has started successfully, you will see the following message printed to the terminal: \n\n        `Serving HTTP on :: port 8080 (http://[::]:8080/) ...`\n\n\n\n1. Select **Make public** in the window that pops up at the bottom right of your Codespace environment.\n\n1. In this Codespace, select the **PORTS** tab. \n\n2. Hover over the **Forwarded Address** column and select the globe icon. This will launch your web app in a new browser tab.\n\n2. Select the **Rewards App (Redirect)** link. You should be redirected to the Okta Sign-in Widget.\n\n3. Select **Sign up** to view the sign-up form you set up.\n\n4. Optionally, complete the sign-up process with values of your choice. The invitation code won't matter since we have not set up validation with an external service yet. This user will automatically be added to the Customers group."
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab Checkpoint",
      "description": "## ✅ Checkpoint\n\nAt this point, you have configured and tested self-service registration for an application."
    }
  ]
}